{{Top}}
[[File:Snowspeeder_2.png|thumb|350px|Two heavy laser cannons point forward on the [[T-47 airspeeder]]]]
'''Laser cannons''' were powerful [[laser]] weapons that were commonly outfitted to vehicles, [[starfighter]]s, and other [[starship]]s,<ref name="SW CVNE" /> emitting a focused laser beam,<ref name="SW EOSAOV (SE)">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles (second edition)]]''</ref> while firing concentrated bolts of energy.<ref name="SW CVNE" /> A laser [[cannon]] could be fixed in place or attached to a [[turret]]<ref name="SWRVG" /> or ball-mounted swivel,<ref name="TLJ VD">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> allowing the weapon to aim and fire in many directions.

==Description==
[[File:Turbolaseronsullust.jpg|thumb|250px|A single-barrel turbolaser turret on an Imperial base|left]]
Laser cannons operated on similar principles as [[blaster]]s and [[blaster cannon]]s &mdash; using high-energy gas to fire concentrated bolts of energy &mdash; but could be more powerful and with greater range. They were the dominant weapon of the [[galaxy]], with a variety of different models mounted on both civilian and military vehicles and vessels.<ref name="SW CVNE">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref>

Like blasters, many laser cannons could vary the intensity of their shots. The laser cannons on a [[UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft]] could be adjusted so that a single shot would reduce a person to ash.<ref name="Victory's Price">''[[Victory's Price: An Alphabet Squadron Novel]]''</ref> The laser cannons on a [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]] could fire bolts of up to 5 gigajoules.<ref name="SW CVNE" />

Laser cannons could also be used to shoot down enemy [[missile]]s.<ref name="ROTSN">[[Star Wars: Revenge of the Sith (novelization)|''Star Wars: Revenge of the Sith'' novelization]]</ref><ref name="Heir">''[[Heir to the Jedi]]''</ref><ref name="Alphabet Squadron">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref><ref name="Shadow Fall">''[[Shadow Fall: An Alphabet Squadron Novel]]''</ref><ref name="Duel of the Droids">{{TCW|Duel of the Droids}}</ref><ref name="Hunted">{{EASWYouTube|f2VmOqjV_7Q|"Hunted"|int=Hunted}}</ref> However doing so required a working [[targeting computer]], as otherwise hitting missiles traveling at extreme velocities could be incredibly hard.<ref name="Shadow Fall" /> Even with a targeting computer, some targets could be very difficult to hit: during the [[Great Hyperspace Disaster]], [[Galactic Republic]] [[Longbeam-class corvette|Longbeam cruiser]] fighters had a one-in-three chance of hitting debris from the ''[[Legacy Run]]'' traveling at close to light-speed.<ref name="The High Republic: Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref>

Manufacturers of laser cannons included [[Sureggi (company)|Sureggi]], whose product was on board the [[Auzituck anti-slaver gunship|''Auzituck'' anti-slaver gunship]].<ref name="SWRVG">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref>

==History==
Vehicles that were equipped with laser cannons included the [[All Terrain Tactical Enforcer]] (AT-TE), the [[All Terrain Armored Transport]] (AT-AT walker), the [[All Terrain Reconnaissance Transport]] (AT-RT), the [[All Terrain Scout Transport]] (AT-ST walker), the [[Gian heavy patrol speeder]], the [[CK-6 swoop bike|freeco bike]], the [[WLO-5 speeder tank|WLO-5 battle tank]], [[General]] [[Grievous]]' [[TSMEU-6 personal wheel bike]], the [[T-47 airspeeder]], and the [[Umbaran mobile heavy cannon]] (MHC).

[[File:DwarfSpiderDroid-SWE.png|thumb|right|250px|Dwarf spider droids were equipped with nose-mounted laser cannons.]]
[[Battle droid]]s that were equipped with laser cannons included the [[DSD1 dwarf spider droid]], which had a [[nose-mounted laser cannon]].<ref name="SWL">{{Legion|set=DSD1 Dwarf Spider Droid Unit Expansion|cardname=Nose-Mounted Laser Cannon}}</ref> 

During a [[skirmish on Florrum]], pirates loyal to their leader [[Hondo Ohnaka]] mounted a laser cannon on a tripod and used it to ambush pirates that had turned against him.<ref name="Revival">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/revival-episode-gallery|text="Revival" Episode Gallery}}; image #14</ref>

==Variants==
===Turbolaser===
{{Main|Turbolaser}}
More powerful versions of laser cannons were [[turbolaser]]s.<ref name="SW CVNE" />

===Rotary laser cannon===
{{Main|Z-6 rotary blaster cannon}}
A type of laser cannon that was used as a personal heavy weapon was referred to as a rotary laser cannon, rotating laser cannon, or as the [[Z-6 rotary blaster cannon]]. Such weapons were used by clone troopers [[Hardcase]]<ref name="Databank Hardcase">{{Databank|hardcase|Clone Trooper Hardcase}}</ref> and [[Thorn]].<ref name="Crisis at the Heart">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/crisis-at-the-heart-episode-gallery|text="Crisis at the Heart" Episode Gallery}}; image #9</ref>

===Heavy, medium and light laser cannons===
{{Main|Heavy laser cannon}}
There were also heavier,<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> medium<ref name="R1VG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> and lighter variants of the standard laser cannon.

